  "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-2ax-3\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-2ay-3\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-2ay-3 \\\\ x+3 & =-2ay \\\\ \\frac{x+3}{2a} & =-y \\\\ -\\frac{x+3}{2a} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\frac{x+3}{2a}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
